 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t an objective single “best” attorney—fit depends on your injuries, the facts, and whether the case may need to go to trial. A few Chicago firms with visible car-accident practices and reported experience include **Salvi, Schostok & Pritchard**, **Levin & Perconti**, **Power Rogers**, and **McDevitt & Cobb**. Their published case results and awards are worth checking, but they’re not guarantees of what your case will recover.\n\nI’d speak with two or three firms before choosing. Ask who will personally handle your case, how much of their work involves car crashes, whether they’ve taken similar cases to trial, and what the fee and case costs are if you don’t recover. Confirm the attorney’s license and standing with the **Illinois Attorney Registration and Disciplinary Commission**. Many firms offer a free initial consultation, so you can compare without committing.",
